@startuml
title Architecture 3: Human-in-the-Loop & Fallback Pattern
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #1F4E79
}

actor "Rider" as Complainant
actor "Operations Admin" as Admin

rectangle "Complaint Ingestion Service" as Ingest
database "Platform DB" as DB

package "AI Orchestration Layer" {
  rectangle "Complaint Analyzer LLM\n(Summary, Severity, Tags)" as Analyzer
  rectangle "Confidence Gate\n(Threshold Monitor)" as ConfGate
}

package "Human-in-the-Loop Governance" {
  rectangle "Admin Review Dashboard" as Dashboard
  rectangle "Disciplinary Execution Engine" as Exec
  database "Audit Service\n(SYS-FR-38)" as Audit
}

Complainant --> Ingest : Submit Complaint
Ingest --> DB : Persist Original Text
Ingest --> Analyzer : Trigger Async Analysis

Analyzer --> ConfGate : AI Result & Recommendation

ConfGate --> Dashboard : [Success & High Confidence]\nPresent AI Analysis + Original
ConfGate --> Dashboard : [Timeout / Low Confidence]\nFallback: Present Original Only

Dashboard --> Admin : Display for Decision
Admin --> Exec : Approve / Reject / Override (Requires Reason)

Exec --> DB : Update Account State (Warning/Suspension)
Exec --> Audit : Log AI Rec vs. Final Human Decision
@enduml